{
  "_comment": [
    "plural-days.json - the report's day counts, in every shipping language.",
    "",
    "The strings are Android's <plurals name=\"days\"> verbatim, with %1$d filled in.",
    "The category each count selects follows CLDR: fr counts 0 as singular, ro adds",
    "few for 0 and 2..19, cs few for 2..4, and pl, ru and uk pick one, few or many",
    "from the last one and two digits. Counts 11..14 and 21..25 are in the list",
    "because that is where those rules part company.",
    "",
    "Android resolves these through getQuantityString and is the authority; iOS",
    "reproduces the selection in DayPlural. Until the 0.84.0 review the iOS report",
    "printed the English forms in every language - a German report read \"8 days\".",
    "",
    "Both suites load this file. A rule written down wrong on one platform shows up",
    "as a mismatch on the other rather than as a plausible-looking wrong word."
  ],
